From fe97efb97173cb496f142f4345b406ce88a340f8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Your Name <you@example.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 23:12:59 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] media: i2c: Add Samsung S5KC505A image sensor driver

Add a V4L2 subdevice driver for the Samsung S5KC505A, a 5 MP
(2608x1960) raw Bayer sensor with an SMIA-style register map and RAW10
output over a 2-lane MIPI CSI-2 D-PHY link.

Supported modes:
  1304x980   2x2 binned, full field of view (default)
  2608x1960  full resolution
  1936x1096  cropped
  1296x736   cropped, 2x2 binned
  640x490    cropped, 4x4 binned

The global and per-mode register settings come from the sensor
configuration in the Lenovo ThinkSmart View (CD-18781Y) Android
firmware; there is no public datasheet. Exposure, analogue gain
(linear, 0x20 = 1x) and vertical blanking are exposed as controls, the
Bayer order is GRBG and the black level is 64 (10-bit).

A newly selected mode defaults to 10 fps through VBLANK, so userspace
that does not manage the frame duration (e.g. the libcamera simple
pipeline) still gets enough exposure time for dim indoor scenes.

Tested on the Lenovo ThinkSmart View (APQ8053, CAMSS CSIPHY0) with
v4l2-ctl raw capture and libcamera (simple pipeline, software ISP).

Signed-off-by: Your Name <you@example.com>
